\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Neuron activation heatmaps comparing visually grounded and hallucinated tokens. \textbf  {Top:} For hallucinated cases, activation patterns remain nearly identical regardless of the visual input's presence, indicating the model is generating text based entirely on language priors. \textbf  {Bottom:} For correctly grounded cases, activation patterns heavily diverge when the image is removed, demonstrating a strong structural reliance on actual visual content.}}{12}{figure.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:neuron}{{2}{12}{Neuron activation heatmaps comparing visually grounded and hallucinated tokens. \textbf {Top:} For hallucinated cases, activation patterns remain nearly identical regardless of the visual input's presence, indicating the model is generating text based entirely on language priors. \textbf {Bottom:} For correctly grounded cases, activation patterns heavily diverge when the image is removed, demonstrating a strong structural reliance on actual visual content}{figure.caption.23}{}}
